                                <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                                    <seg type="script">18th-century script</seg>
                                    <date notBefore="1700" notAfter="1799"/>      
                                    <seg type="ink">Black, red</seg>
                                    <desc>
                                        Some paleographic features:
                                        the upper parts of ቆ, ቶ, የ, ደ have angular shape;
                                        the left stroke of ዘ is curved;
                                        the vowel marker of ብ is placed on top of the letter.
                                    </desc>
                                    <seg type="rubrication">Titles.</seg>
                                </handNote>
                            </handDesc>
                            
                            <additions>
                                <list>
                                    <item xml:id="e1">
                                        <desc>
                                            The name of several individuals are mentioned, possibly owners of the manuscript. 
                                            The first name is partially illegible due to erasure. The cataloguers read <foreign xml:lang="gez">ብ<gap reason="illegible"/>፡ አቤል</foreign> (<locus target="#130v #169r #180r"/>). 
                                            The name of another individual, <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15037Falaski">Falaskinos Bagādā Ṣǝyon</persName>, appears from <locus target="#141v"/> onwards. 
                                            The name of the third owner, <persName role="owner" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15038WaldaMa">Walda Masqal</persName>, only appears on <locus target="#82v #83r"/>.
                                        </desc>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </additions>
                            
